license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Research software for a retrospective simulated market backtest using an
  Ikeda-type delay reservoir, an expanding-window ridge readout, and a
  volatility-scaled portfolio rule. On a fixed 628-session holdout spanning
  2024-01-02 through 2026-07-06, the nine-instrument simulated portfolio
  produced a 5.7199 percent net return under the stated cost rule, with a net
  Sharpe ratio of 1.3930, maximum drawdown of -1.6863 percent, and an
  elapsed-calendar-time Calmar ratio of 1.3299. These historical simulation
  statistics are not live performance or a guarantee of future results.
keywords:
  - reservoir computing
  - Ikeda delay system
  - time-series prediction
  - simulated backtesting
  - walk-forward validation
  - Calmar ratio
